      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "So, let's finally take a look at this in more detail.\n\n@Andrew Wingate The reticle stitcher does not differentiate between a saw street and a callout. Everything between two user projects is designated as the saw street, so the only relevant factor for me is the total width required.\n\nDo I see it right that the initial suggestion from them was 100um saw street + 2*150um callout? That would be 400um in total? That's huge...\n\nEven if we rotated the reticle by 90° and lost a few slots that way, Tim showed that we can only get to a 281um total saw street. Otherwise, we would have to remove a column of projects.\n\nI also see a 75um callout in your sketch. Would 100um + 2*75um also be an option they can work with? i.e. 250um in total?",
      "author": {
        "id": "323371864074485771",
        "name": "mole99",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Leo Moser (mole99)",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
