      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Thanks for the reply.\n\nSorry but your sketch is a bit hard to read. I only see 100um as the saw street width, not for the callout? Or did you mean to say 150um instead of 100um?\n\nSo 75um callout with backgrinding, and 150um callout without backgrinding? And the saw street is always fixed at 100um.\n\nBut then again, is backside chipping such a big deal to us? Also, to keep this in relation, we are now doing 60um total width with backgrinding, which is significantly smaller than what they would like and it still seems to work reliable for Run 1-3 on their end?",
